  "operation": {
    "name": "OPERATION SEA SERPENT",
    "taskForce": "77th JSOC · TASK FORCE TRIDENT",
    "version": "SHOWCASE 1.0",
    "briefing": "ARMA REFORGER / EVERON — FICTIONAL GAME SCENARIO\n\nMISSION: Task Force Trident establishes a foothold, secures Meaux harbour (OBJ ANCHOR), and takes control of the northern airfield (OBJ CROWN). Recover the intelligence package and extract the designated role-play HVT.\n\nPHASE I — RECON & INSERT: RAVEN observes the northern sector; REAPER and the green FIA liaison establish observation points. EAGLE inserts the recon element at LZ VIPER. ALPHA assembles at FOB TRIDENT.\nPHASE II — HARBOUR: ALPHA 1/2 move along the blue planning corridor to OBJ ANCHOR. BRAVO holds the reserve. SAPPER checks the marked hazard area. DOC establishes the casualty collection point.\nPHASE III — AIRFIELD: BRAVO advances along AXIS CROWN after the scenario controller confirms the harbour objective. REAPER links up from the flank. Recover INTEL and escort HVT to the pickup point. HAMMER remains a scenario-controlled support reserve: its area is a staging boundary, not a ballistic range card.\nPHASE IV — EXTRACT: EAGLE follows the purple corridor to LZ HOME. Use the amber alternate route if the main route is unavailable. Account for all elements and return to FOB TRIDENT.\n\nBRIEFING CONTROLS: Brief → mission phases toggles each stage; shared markers are persistent command, objectives and scenario opposition. Units → command tree expands ACTUAL, ALPHA, BRAVO and aviation. Draw selects named routes/areas for editing. Presentation export → spread overlapping units is useful for an overview.\n\nLEGEND: Blue = friendly; red = fictional scenario opposition; green = independent FIA; purple = aviation/recon; orange = hazards/alternate route; white = civilian or landing landmark. Dashed = movement corridor; arrow = advance; dotted = alternate/recon.\n\nASSETS: Assigned catalog records use installed mod names and Workshop IDs: 77th JSOC Patches, RHS - Status Quo, Dax Humvees, Sikorsky H60 Project, RiptideMQ9, M270 MLRS, ZU-23, GM Editable Intel, ACE Medical Core. These are mod references, not verified spawned entities or exact prefabs. No naval fleet or carrier asset is claimed.\n\nMAP NOTE: Positions and waypoint corridors are illustrative planning placements on the Everon imagery. Check terrain, road bends and landing suitability in-game. Airfield and Meaux sectors follow the previous user-tested locations. This JSON creates a plan only; it does not spawn missions or send orders to Reforger. LIVE and Simulation remain separate overlays."
  },
